WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:07.740
Air pollution, energy insecurity, and global&nbsp;
warming - fixing these huge problems may seem&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:12.780
impossible. But we don't need a miracle. We&nbsp;
can save our Earth and clean our air and we can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:18.840
start right now using the technology we already&nbsp;
have. I'm Mark Jacobson, a Professor of civil and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:24.180
environmental engineering at Stanford University.&nbsp;
In this course I'll take you inside my classroom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:28.500
and share the science and strategies for building&nbsp;
clean renewable energy and storage for everything.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:34.620
From our transportation system and electricity&nbsp;
infrastructure, to our industries and businesses&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:39.960
you will learn about the key technologies for&nbsp;
harnessing the power of the wind, the water,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:45.600
and the sun with storage to meet all our energy&nbsp;
needs. You will also learn how to make power grids&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:51.000
efficient, resilient, and dependable anywhere in&nbsp;
the world, and how to develop and Implement a road&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.100
map to transition your country, state, community,&nbsp;
or business to 100 clean renewable energy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.620
You don't have to be a scientist or an engineer.&nbsp;
These lessons are for anyone who wants to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:06.720
understand the latest research about what works&nbsp;
what doesn't and why. We'll explain everything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:11.760
from photovoltaics, to hydroelectricity, to wind&nbsp;
turbines, to batteries, to electrolyzers, to heat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:17.100
pumps, and show you why renewable electricity&nbsp;
generation and storage won't just save our planet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:22.800
it'll also create new job opportunities from&nbsp;
energy to manufacturing. Whether you work in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.960
business, government, education, or the nonprofit&nbsp;
sector this foundational course will give you the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:31.740
practical knowledge you need to communicate&nbsp;
about those important issues with confidence,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:35.220
transform your organization, and&nbsp;
contribute to a healthier planet.

